<PolicyLayout title="Privacy policy" description="How MyChristianTutors uses and protects family, student, tutor and booking information.">
  <p>MyChristianTutors uses personal information to answer inquiries, arrange tutoring, process orders and support families and tutors. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:admin@mychristiantutors.com">admin@mychristiantutors.com</a>. We reply to all emails within 24 hours.</p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact details:</strong> the name, email address, phone number and messages you provide through our forms or when booking.</li>
    <li><strong>Tutoring details:</strong> student names entered by the family, selected subjects and tutors, package hours, session dates and times, time zone and meeting instructions.</li>
    <li><strong>Order records:</strong> payment status, amounts, discounts and payment-provider references. Stripe handles card payments; our site does not store your full card number or security code.</li>
    <li><strong>Tutor information:</strong> profile and contact details, subjects, availability, meeting instructions, and application information such as qualifications, teaching experience and approach.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical information:</strong> information used by our hosting and security services, such as IP addresses, browser information, request logs and errors. Our request-limit records use a keyed hash of the network address rather than storing the raw address in those records.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Please provide only what we need to arrange tutoring. A student’s first name is sufficient for planning. Do not send card details, identity documents or sensitive student records through a contact form.</p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <p>We use your information to respond to you, match students with tutors, reserve times, process and record payments, send booking details and service messages, handle schedule changes and billing questions, and protect the site from misuse. We do not sell personal information or use it for targeted advertising.</p>
  <p>Where privacy law requires a legal basis, we rely on providing the service you request, meeting legal obligations and our legitimate interests in operating and securing the service. Where consent is required for a particular use, we will ask for it separately.</p>

  <h2>Who receives information</h2>
  <p>Admin staff and the tutors involved in your inquiry or booking receive the information needed to respond and provide tutoring. This can include family contact details, student names, subjects, schedules and information you choose to share about learning needs.</p>
  <p>We use service providers to operate the website: Vercel for hosting, Neon for database storage, Stripe for payments, Resend for email delivery and Google Workspace for our email inbox. These providers process information needed for their services. Booking emails and inquiries may also remain in the relevant inboxes.</p>
  <p>The website loads fonts from Google Fonts. Your browser connects to Google to retrieve those fonts, which exposes technical information such as your IP address to Google. Online sessions may use a tutor’s chosen meeting provider; that provider’s own privacy terms apply to its service. We may also disclose information when required by law or to protect people and the service.</p>

  <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
  <p>We use an essential cookie for admin sign-in. Checkout uses browser session storage to retain a random request identifier and a fingerprint of the plan so retries can reuse the same checkout. That stored entry does not contain the family’s contact details. Blocking essential storage may affect these features. We do not place advertising cookies.</p>

  <h2>Children’s information</h2>
  <p>This website’s booking and contact forms are intended for parents, guardians and adults, rather than for children to use independently. Parents or guardians provide the student information needed for tutoring and should manage communications and bookings for children.</p>
  <p>If you believe a child submitted personal information directly without a parent’s involvement, contact us. We will investigate and remove information where appropriate. Parents and guardians can also ask us to review, correct or delete information about their child, subject to necessary recordkeeping and legal requirements.</p>

  <h2>Storage, security and retention</h2>
  <p>We restrict access to information needed to operate the service and use encrypted connections for the website and its hosted services. No online system can guarantee complete security.</p>
  <p>We retain booking, payment and correspondence records as needed to provide tutoring, support customers, meet accounting or legal obligations and resolve disputes. Information in provider backups and email inboxes may follow their own retention schedules. Contact us about deletion; some records may need to be retained for those purposes.</p>
  <p>Our providers may process information in the United States and other countries. Privacy laws in those countries may differ from those where you live. Contact admin if you have questions about where your information is processed or the protections used.</p>

  <h2>Your choices and requests</h2>
  <p>Contact admin to ask about access, correction or deletion of your information. Depending on where you live, you may also have rights to restrict or object to processing, request a portable copy, withdraw consent for uses that rely on consent, or complain to a privacy regulator. We may need to verify your identity before handling a request.</p>
  <p>Service emails about bookings, payments and inquiries are separate from optional marketing. We will ask separately before adding you to a marketing mailing list. Links to other websites, including MyFunScience, are governed by those websites’ own privacy notices.</p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>We will update the date at the top of this page when this notice changes and provide further notice where required. Email <a href="mailto:admin@mychristiantutors.com">admin@mychristiantutors.com</a> with questions. Our <a href="/booking-policy">Booking, cancellation and refund policy</a> explains the terms for tutoring purchases.</p>
</PolicyLayout>
